{"timestamp":"2026-05-09T04:42:00+01:00","topic":"debug-ui-control-grammar","lesson":"Aquarium debug UI uses a code-first Direct2D/DirectWrite overlay with explicit bound controls. Rect math must distinguish edges from width/height, controls need base/hover/active feedback, tooltips live in declarations, and long mode selectors should be named option rows instead of numeric sliders.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Ui/DebugUi.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-09T05:20:00+01:00","topic":"graphics-settings-cultcache","lesson":"Renderer presentation knobs belong in a typed CultCache graphics settings document, not process folklore. Current durable knobs are render debug mode, exposure, bloom intensity, and bloom veil.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine.Contracts/GraphicsSettings.cs","src/Aquarium.Epiphany/State/AquariumGraphicsSettingsState.cs","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-12T00:00:00+01:00","topic":"engine-client-boundary","lesson":"Aquarium.Engine is the native D3D12/window/render graph layer and must not accrete Epiphany frontend semantics. Aquarium.Epiphany is the client/runtime layer behind Aquarium.Engine.Contracts and should configure engine abstractions for cameras, targets, shaders, resources, and passes.","files":["docs/engine-client-boundary.md","src/Aquarium.Epiphany/Aquarium.Epiphany.csproj","src/Aquarium.Engine/Runtime/ClientRuntimeLoader.cs","state/memory.json","state/map.yaml"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-12T00:00:00+01:00","topic":"epiphany-extraction-render-api-plan","lesson":"The next purification path is a small render graph API, not more renderer knobs: clients declare resources and passes, Aquarium owns D3D12 execution. Migrate in slices: freeze boundary, add Vortice-free descriptors, compile a minimal graph, convert presentation/bloom, move Epiphany body shaders and Grid policy to Aquarium.Epiphany, then replace AquariumFrame.","files":["docs/epiphany-extraction-render-api-plan.md","README.md","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-12T03:40:00+01:00","topic":"epiphany-render-policy-extraction","lesson":"Epiphany body shaders, Grid brush construction, body visual/light tables, and cursor projection moved behind Aquarium.Engine.Contracts. Aquarium.Engine now consumes AquariumRenderPlan and AquariumSceneState data and passes scripts/verify-boundaries.ps1 with no Epiphany role/client names in engine source.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine.Contracts/Render/AquariumApp.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine.Contracts/Render/AquariumRenderPlan.cs","src/Aquarium.Epiphany/EpiphanyRenderPlan.cs","src/Aquarium.Epiphany/EpiphanySceneBuilder.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","scripts/verify-boundaries.ps1","state/memory.json","state/map.yaml"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-12T03:50:00+01:00","topic":"graph-target-allocation","lesson":"The render graph compiler now validates declared targets/passes and D3D12Renderer allocates non-legacy client-declared render targets through engine resource/descriptors, including resize rebuild. This is allocation only; full graph pass execution remains the next cut.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Graph/D3D12RenderGraphCompiler.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine.Contracts/Render/AquariumApp.cs","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-12T04:00:00+01:00","topic":"minimal-non-epiphany-client","lesson":"Aquarium now includes src/Aquarium.Sample.Minimal, a non-Epiphany client that references only Aquarium.Engine.Contracts, declares a minimal render plan, and boots through the same host/client assembly loader. Keep it as a boundary proof while the graph executor replaces legacy fixed passes.","files":["src/Aquarium.Sample.Minimal/MinimalRuntime.cs","src/Aquarium.Sample.Minimal/Aquarium.Sample.Minimal.csproj","README.md","state/map.yaml"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-12T04:05:00+01:00","topic":"grid-brush-gpu-packing","lesson":"GridHeightBrushConstants is D3D12 GPU packing for the height-field brush pass, not scene policy. Keep brush authoring in the client, keep packing in engine feature code, and keep D3D12Renderer limited to upload/command recording until the height-field pass moves fully into the graph executor.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Features/D3D12GridHeightBrushConstants.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","state/evidence.jsonl"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-10T07:47:46+01:00","topic":"cursor-teardrop-sdf","lesson":"Use the MathWorld teardrop curve for the cursor profile with m=6, revolved into an SDF locator. Keep ripples as geometry, material as brass GGX metal, and avoid ambient fill.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","state/memory.json"],"source":"https://mathworld.wolfram.com/TeardropCurve.html"}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T00:00:00+01:00","topic":"aquarium-focus-cut","lesson":"Runtime volumetrics, cloud/fog research, and the D3D11 scene renderer are shelved because they distract from Aquarium's Epiphany-client mission. Git history holds the experiment; live repo state should not preserve compatibility husks or dead guidance for removed medium settings.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine.Contracts/GraphicsSettings.cs","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json","state/scratch.md"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T04:20:00+01:00","topic":"medium-froxel-purge","lesson":"Medium/froxel render targets, structured buffers, shader bindings, scene outputs, post history lanes, and medium debug paths were removed from the live D3D12 renderer. Future atmospheric or field transport work needs a new explicit pass contract rather than reviving shelved scaffolding.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Post.hlsl","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T05:32:00+01:00","topic":"body-light-lane","lesson":"Blue-noise assets are retained for future dithering. Self and future other Selves emit through an explicit body light buffer; generic field instances are not the lighting authority.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T06:18:00+01:00","topic":"pmrem-cubemap-bake","lesson":"Studio HDR reflection lighting is baked as a PMREM DDS cubemap: roughness selects higher mips, and the bake samples the source latlong by output direction so cubemap faces are generated from one continuous domain instead of filtered as isolated square images.","files":["scripts/bake-pmrem-cubemap.py","src/Aquarium.Engine/Assets/Textures/studio3_pmrem.dds","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json"],"source":"E:\\Projects\\EpiphanyAquarium\\public\\textures\\studio3.hdr"}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T06:28:00+01:00","topic":"pmrem-scene-binding","lesson":"The Studio3 PMREM asset is live in the scene as a D3D12 TextureCube bound at t22. The renderer owns a narrow RGBA16F DX10 DDS cubemap loader, keeps upload resources alive until the copy fence completes, and the scene shader uses roughness-scaled SampleLevel for specular material reflections only.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12CubeTexture.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T06:42:00+01:00","topic":"grid-mirror-surface","lesson":"Grid linework was replaced with a terminating perfect mirror surface. Grid hits now write the primary scene packet with FIELD_ID_GRID, terrain normal, full coverage, and Studio3 PMREM mip 0 reflection instead of using the transparent event lane.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T06:50:00+01:00","topic":"pmrem-world-basis","lesson":"Aquarium world space is Z-up while the baked Studio3 PMREM cubemap is sampled as Y-up. Every PMREM lookup must convert world directions with (x, z, y) before TextureCube sampling, or the HDRI appears sideways.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:00:00+01:00","topic":"studio2-pmrem-probe","lesson":"Active reflection probe switched to Studio2 from E:\\Projects\\Aetheria-Economy\\Assets\\Textures\\studio2.hdr. The renderer loads Assets/Textures/studio2_pmrem.dds through the existing D3D12 TextureCube PMREM path, and the unused Studio3 DDS was cut from live assets.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Assets/Textures/studio2_pmrem.dds","src/Aquarium.Engine/Assets/Textures/studio3_pmrem.dds","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json"],"source":"E:\\Projects\\Aetheria-Economy\\Assets\\Textures\\studio2.hdr"}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:14:00+01:00","topic":"grid-brush-cpu-mirror","lesson":"Self's Grid gravity bowl now uses a 17-world-unit radius and an Aetheria-style radial cosine wave. The brush equation is mirrored across D3D12Grid, CPU body-light placement, D3D12Scene body centers, and D3D12Post temporal reprojection; body centers sit at Grid height plus 2x radius.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Grid.hlsl","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Post.hlsl","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json"],"source":"E:\\Projects\\Aetheria-Economy\\Assets\\Shaders\\Brushes\\RadialWaveBrush.shader"}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:22:00+01:00","topic":"grid-flatness-roughness","lesson":"Grid reflection roughness is now slope-driven: flat regions sample higher Studio2 PMREM mips to avoid an over-literal HDRI mirror, while sloped or waved regions sharpen toward mip 0.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:28:00+01:00","topic":"pmrem-background-mip","lesson":"Flat Grid reflection now tops out at Studio2 PMREM mip 3, and ray misses use Studio2 PMREM mip 3 as the soft background so the reflective Grid is not contrasted against black void. Low-resolution mip texels are hidden with a small multi-direction cone average rather than one magnified TextureCube sample.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","state/memory.json"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:36:00+01:00","topic":"studio2-pmrem-resolution","lesson":"Studio2 PMREM was rebaked at 512px per cubemap face with 10 mips, so mip 3 is 64px per face instead of 32px. Shader roughness LOD max moved to 9 to match the chain.","files":["src/Aquarium.Engine/Assets/Textures/studio2_pmrem.dds","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","state/memory.json"],"source":"E:\\Projects\\Aetheria-Economy\\Assets\\Textures\\studio2.hdr"}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:45:00+01:00","topic":"diffuse-ibl-irradiance","lesson":"Diffuse IBL is not GGX PMREM with a softer mip. Studio2 diffuse lighting now uses a separate irradiance cubemap baked by cosine-weighted hemisphere convolution, stores the Li*cos(theta) irradiance integral, and shades non-metal bodies with Fresnel-gated albedo/PI diffuse response.","files":["scripts/bake-pmrem-cubemap.py","src/Aquarium.Engine/Assets/Textures/studio2_irradiance.dds","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/D3D12Renderer.cs","src/Aquarium.Engine/Render/Shaders/D3D12Scene.hlsl","state/map.yaml","state/memory.json"],"source":"E:\\Projects\\Aetheria-Economy\\Assets\\Textures\\studio2.hdr"}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:10:00+01:00","topic":"rider-solution-compatibility","lesson":"Rider may open Aquarium.Engine.slnx with empty project trees even though dotnet can build it. Keep Aquarium.Engine.sln as the Rider-facing classic solution while Aquarium.Engine.slnx remains the compact CLI solution.","files":["Aquarium.Engine.sln","Aquarium.Engine.slnx","README.md","state/map.yaml"]}
